&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Legal Counsel Corporate &amp;amp; Regulatory to strengthen our expertise in corporate law and banking regulation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together with your team, you will advise internal stakeholders on a broad range of legal matters across Corporate Law, Corporate Governance, M&amp;amp;A, Corporate Financing and, prospectively, Capital Markets Law. Another key element of your role will be advising on banking regulatory matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with your team, our management and our General Counsel, you will develop pragmatic solutions across a broad range of topics. You will also work closely with external counsel and independently coordinate their work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will join the Corporate / Regulatory Team within our Legal Department and have the exciting opportunity to further develop our Corporate Law function in a fast-growing company operating in a highly regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your work will focus on Corporate Governance (in particular, supporting the General Meeting, Supervisory Board and Management Board), Corporate Financing and M&amp;amp;A. You will work closely with the Head of Corporate Law and various stakeholders across the N26 Group.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will identify and assess legal and business risks, develop strategies to address them and provide pragmatic and creative support in their implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will work closely and cross-functionally with Finance, the Executive Office and the Banking Team on matters relating to the areas of law outlined above. This will also include advising on employee participation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will independently support complex national and international transactions as well as our planned IPO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In everything you do, you will ensure that applicable regulatory requirements are appropriately considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you should bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have completed both German state law examinations (&lt;em&gt;Staatsexamen&lt;/em&gt;) with above-average results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have at least two years of professional experience in Corporate Law, particularly German stock corporation law (&lt;em&gt;Aktienrecht&lt;/em&gt;), gained at a renowned law firm and/or an international company, ideally in the financial sector.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have gained initial experience in banking regulatory law or are motivated to develop expertise in this area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong interest in technology, business and digital business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work independently and in a highly structured manner, make decisions and are prepared to stand behind them both internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are willing to take a pragmatic approach to familiarizing yourself with new topics and areas of law and to closely follow dynamic regulatory developments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to communicate complex matters and legal considerations clearly and appropriately for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate a high level of integrity, commitment and initiative and are comfortable taking responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
